  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f5e86851-b0b9-5b1c-bd5e-f3b23ea16f4e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Užupis, Freetown Christiania, Belmontas, Rasos, Copenhagen, Paris\n- People: Christian Skeel\n- Topics: artists, bohemic atmosphere, laissez-faire atmosphere, public closure, location\n\nFacts:\n- Užupis has been popular with artists for some time.\n- Užupis has been compared to Montmartre in Paris because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- Užupis has also been compared to Freetown Christiania in Copenhagen because of its bohemic and laissez-faire atmosphere.\n- In April 2011, residents temporarily closed Freetown Christiania while discussions with the Danish government about its future continued.\n- After the April 2011 closure, Freetown Christiania re-opened to the public.\n- Belmontas is located in the area of Rasos on the right bank of the Vilnia River, east of Užupis.\n- Christian Skeel lives and works in Copenhagen.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
